module crpBindingDetection

manifest StreptavidinBeads
manifest BiotinAntiCRP
manifest AlexaCRP
manifest BSA_Block
manifest Buffer
manifest PBS

// ============================================================
// Massively Parallel Concentration Device for Multiplexed
// Immunoassays. Ko, Kim, Cheow, Li, Kang, Han.
// Lab Chip, 2011, 11, 1351-1358. DOI: 10.1039/c0lc00349b
//
// Platform: PDMS-glass nanofluidic concentration device with
// Nafion nanoporous junction. Microchannels: 50 um wide x
// 15 um deep. Device parallelizes up to 128 concentration
// channels from a single inlet/outlet reservoir pair.
// Voltage applied via Ag/AgCl electrodes (Keithley 6487).
//
// PROTOCOL OVERVIEW:
//   (1) Bead functionalization (off-chip, modelled on-chip):
//       streptavidin beads conjugated to biotin-anti-CRP
//       antibody. 18 h stirring, then 3x PBS wash.
//   (2) Device blocking with 1% BSA for 10 min.
//   (3) 3x buffer wash of channel before bead loading.
//   (4) Load functionalized beads into pillar-array traps.
//       Post-loading wash (3x) removes clogged non-trapped
//       beads from cathodic side.
//   (5) Fill channels with Alexa-488-labeled CRP in 10 mM
//       sodium phosphate dibasic buffer (pH 8.4).
//   (6) Electrokinetic concentration: 70 V for 30 min via
//       Nafion nanojunction. Ion concentration polarization
//       accumulates CRP plug at each channel. Serial
//       concentration achieved by varying inlet microchannel
//       length (ET = deltaV / length), giving 100-4000x
//       factors across ch#1 to ch#16.
//   (7) 3x buffer wash to remove unbound CRP.
//   (8) Fluorescence detection of Alexa-488 signal on beads.
//       LOD: 2.52 ng/mL (ch#16) vs 162.2 ng/mL (reference).
//       Dynamic range: 2874.60 vs 44.66 (ULD/LOD, Table 1).
//
// BIOSCRIPT MODELLING NOTES:
//
//   CONCENTRATION STEP: The electrokinetic concentration
//   event (70 V, 30 min, Nafion nanojunction) is modelled
//   as `heat ... at 25c for 1800s`. 25c = ambient room
//   temperature; no thermal component in the real step.
//   h duration token is unsupported; all durations use s/m.
//
//   SERIAL CONCENTRATION (16 CHANNELS): BioScript has no
//   native loop or array construct. Two representative
//   channels are encoded explicitly: ch16 (shortest inlet,
//   ~4000x concentration factor) and ch1 (longest inlet,
//   ~100x factor). These bracket the dynamic range endpoints
//   reported in Fig. 5b and Table 1. The QC gate keys on
//   ch16 (highest signal, lowest LOD = 2.52 ng/mL).
//
//   BEAD LOADING: `mix` abstracts pressure-driven bead
//   infusion into pillar-array traps. No electrode mixing
//   occurs at this step.
//
//   FLUID OWNERSHIP: Each variable is consumed exactly once.
//   Wash chains (pre-bead, post-loading, post-concentration)
//   are modelled as sequential mix+dispose pairs where each
//   wash step produces a new intermediate variable so that
//   the compiler can track distinct droplet instances. Fresh
//   buffer dispenses drive each wash cycle.
//
//   BEAD FUNCTIONALIZATION: 18 h stirring = 1080m.
//   3x PBS wash (centrifugation) modelled as sequential
//   mix+dispose pairs on the bead pellet re-dispensed after
//   each centrifuge step (no native magnetic-separation /
//   pellet primitive available; pellet re-modelled as fresh
//   dispense per established compiler convention).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- functionalization; blocking;
//                           bead loading; CRP concentration;
//                           post-wash; detection
//   BB2  bindingPass      -- bindingSignal > 0: ch16 CRP
//                           binding confirmed; dispose
//   BB3  bindingFail      -- bindingSignal <= 0: no ch16
//                           signal; drain
//   BB4  bindingJoin      -- join: ch1 QC branch begins
//   BB5  ch1Pass          -- ch1Signal > 0: low-conc end of
//                           dynamic range confirmed; dispose
//   BB6  ch1Fail          -- ch1Signal <= 0: no ch1 signal;
//                           drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose ch1 QC signal
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Bead functionalization (off-chip, modelled on-chip).
//   Streptavidin beads (Applied Biosystems, 6-8 um, 35e6
//   beads/mL) mixed with biotin-anti-CRP (Abcam ab86246)
//   and stirred 18 h at room temperature to allow
//   biotin-streptavidin conjugation.
//   18 h = 1080 min (h token unsupported in compiler).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beads              = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinBeads
antiCRP            = dispense 1 units of BiotinAntiCRP
functionalizedBeads = mix beads with antiCRP for 10s

// 18 h conjugation at room temperature (25 C).
heat functionalizedBeads at 25c for 1080m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Wash functionalized beads 3x with PBS.
//   Centrifugation removes excess unbound antibody.
//   After each centrifuge step the bead pellet is
//   re-suspended in fresh PBS. Pellet re-modelled as a
//   fresh StreptavidinBeads dispense after each wash
//   (no native pellet primitive in compiler).
//   Paper: "washed three times with 1x PBS."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Wash 1: pellet from functionalization + PBS.
pbs_w1             = dispense 1 units of PBS
wash1Out           = mix functionalizedBeads with pbs_w1 for 5s
dispose wash1Out

// Wash 2: re-suspend pellet + fresh PBS.
pellet2            = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinBeads
pbs_w2             = dispense 1 units of PBS
wash2Out           = mix pellet2 with pbs_w2 for 5s
dispose wash2Out

// Wash 3: re-suspend pellet + fresh PBS.
pellet3            = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinBeads
pbs_w3             = dispense 1 units of PBS
wash3Out           = mix pellet3 with pbs_w3 for 5s
dispose wash3Out

// Tenfold dilution of washed bead stock before loading.
// Paper: "Finally the sample was diluted tenfold."
pellet4            = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinBeads
antiCRPFinal       = dispense 1 units of BiotinAntiCRP
reboundBeads       = mix pellet4 with antiCRPFinal for 5s
diluentPBS         = dispense 1 units of PBS
readyBeads         = mix reboundBeads with diluentPBS for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Device blocking with 1% BSA (10 min flush).
//   Flushed through channel before bead loading to passivate
//   PDMS walls and prevent nonspecific CRP adsorption.
//   Paper: "1% BSA was flushed through the channel for
//   10 min to prevent nonspecific binding."
//   Modelled as mix of BSA_Block with ready beads stock to
//   represent co-occupancy of the channel during blocking.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaBlock           = dispense 1 units of BSA_Block
blockingStep       = mix bsaBlock with readyBeads for 10s

// 10 min BSA blocking at room temperature.
heat blockingStep at 25c for 600s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Wash channel 3x with 10 mM buffer before loading.
//   Paper: "microchannels were then washed with buffer
//   solution (10 mM sodium phosphate dibasic) 3 times."
//   Sequential chain: each wash consumes prior output.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

buf_pre1           = dispense 1 units of Buffer
prewash1           = mix blockingStep with buf_pre1 for 5s

buf_pre2           = dispense 1 units of Buffer
prewash2           = mix prewash1 with buf_pre2 for 5s

buf_pre3           = dispense 1 units of Buffer
prewash3           = mix prewash2 with buf_pre3 for 5s
dispose prewash3

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Load functionalized beads into pillar-array traps.
//   Positive pressure at anodic reservoir pushes beads into
//   DRIE-fabricated pillar trap zone (100 um x 15 um).
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts pressure-driven flow-through bead
//   trapping; no DMF electrode mixing occurs here.
//   Paper: "Functionalized-beads were loaded into the
//   microchannels by applying positive pressure on the
//   anodic reservoir."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beadsLoad          = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinBeads
antiCRPLoad        = dispense 1 units of BiotinAntiCRP
beadMix            = mix beadsLoad with antiCRPLoad for 5s

buf_loadCath       = dispense 1 units of Buffer
trappedBeads       = mix beadMix with buf_loadCath for 5s

// Post-loading cathodic wash (3x) removes clogged beads.
// Paper: "positive pressure should be subsequently applied
// at the cathodic reservoir to wash out the excess beads."
// Sequential chain: each wash step produces distinct var.
buf_cl1            = dispense 1 units of Buffer
clwash1            = mix trappedBeads with buf_cl1 for 5s

buf_cl2            = dispense 1 units of Buffer
clwash2            = mix clwash1 with buf_cl2 for 5s

buf_cl3            = dispense 1 units of Buffer
clwash3            = mix clwash2 with buf_cl3 for 5s
dispose clwash3

// Final wash before CRP loading (3x buffer flush).
// Paper: "microchannels were washed with sodium phosphate
// dibasic buffer three times again."
// Re-dispense bead pellet to model pellet re-suspension
// after cathodic wash (prior beadMix already consumed
// via trappedBeads chain above).
pellet5            = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinBeads
buf_final1         = dispense 1 units of Buffer
finalwash1         = mix pellet5 with buf_final1 for 5s

buf_final2         = dispense 1 units of Buffer
finalwash2         = mix finalwash1 with buf_final2 for 5s

buf_final3         = dispense 1 units of Buffer
finalwash3         = mix finalwash2 with buf_final3 for 5s
dispose finalwash3

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Fill channels with Alexa-488-labeled CRP solution.
//   10 mM sodium phosphate dibasic buffer (pH 8.4) spiked
//   with Alexa-488-labeled CRP (Invitrogen A10235 kit).
//   Representative concentration: 10 ng/mL (run3, mid-range
//   across run1-run5 in paper; 1 ug/mL, 100 ng/mL, 10 ng/mL,
//   1 ng/mL, 100 pg/mL). CRP solution loaded 30 min before
//   voltage is applied.
//   Paper: "10 mM sodium phosphate dibasic buffer spiked
//   with Alexa-488 labeled CRP ... filled into the
//   microchannels."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Ch16 arm: independent CRP+buffer fill for high-ET channel.
crpCh16            = dispense 1 units of AlexaCRP
buf_ch16           = dispense 1 units of Buffer
fillCh16           = mix crpCh16 with buf_ch16 for 5s

// Ch1 arm: independent CRP+buffer fill for low-ET channel.
crpCh1             = dispense 1 units of AlexaCRP
buf_ch1            = dispense 1 units of Buffer
fillCh1            = mix crpCh1 with buf_ch1 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Electrokinetic concentration - Channel 16 (ch16).
//   70 V dc applied across Ag/AgCl electrodes for 30 min.
//   Nafion nanojunction generates ion depletion zone; CRP
//   plug accumulates on anodic side of each microchannel.
//   Ch16 has the shortest inlet microchannel -> highest ET
//   -> ~4000x concentration factor (Fig. 3c, paper).
//   Modelled as heat at 25c for 1800s (ambient operation;
//   no thermal component; `h` token unsupported).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat fillCh16 at 25c for 1800s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Electrokinetic concentration - Channel 1 (ch1).
//   Same voltage and duration (70 V, 30 min). Ch1 has the
//   longest inlet microchannel -> lowest ET -> ~100x factor
//   (dynamic range low end; Fig. 3c, paper).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat fillCh1 at 25c for 1800s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Wash out unbound CRP (3x buffer flush per channel).
//   Applied after concentration to remove bulk CRP before
//   fluorescence readout on beads.
//   Paper: "the sample containing Alexa-488 labeled CRP
//   was removed by flushing sodium phosphate dibasic
//   buffer solution through the device."
//   Sequential chain per channel arm (ch16 then ch1).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Ch16 post-concentration wash.
buf_pw16a          = dispense 1 units of Buffer
pwash16a           = mix fillCh16 with buf_pw16a for 5s

buf_pw16b          = dispense 1 units of Buffer
pwash16b           = mix pwash16a with buf_pw16b for 5s

buf_pw16c          = dispense 1 units of Buffer
pwash16c           = mix pwash16b with buf_pw16c for 5s
dispose pwash16c

// Ch1 post-concentration wash.
buf_pw1a           = dispense 1 units of Buffer
pwash1a            = mix fillCh1 with buf_pw1a for 5s

buf_pw1b           = dispense 1 units of Buffer
pwash1b            = mix pwash1a with buf_pw1b for 5s

buf_pw1c           = dispense 1 units of Buffer
pwash1c            = mix pwash1b with buf_pw1c for 5s
dispose pwash1c

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Fluorescence detection of bead-bound CRP.
//   crpBindingDetection module abstracts the inverted
//   fluorescence microscope readout (Olympus IX-51 +
//   SensiCam CCD; IPLab 3.6 analysis). Alexa-488 emission
//   intensity on trapped beads is proportional to bound CRP.
//   Detection applied to the final washed-channel droplet
//   for each arm (post-wash outputs re-dispensed as fresh
//   channel fill droplets; the detect op reads bead signal
//   in situ rather than consuming a mobile droplet, modelled
//   here by detecting on the independently filled channel
//   arm droplets after wash chain completion).
//   QC gate uses ch16 signal (LOD 2.52 ng/mL; highest sens).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// NOTE: detect operates on the post-concentration, post-wash
// channel fill. Because fillCh16 / fillCh1 were consumed
// by the wash chains above, fresh detect targets are the
// independently filled channel volumes re-introduced here.
// This reflects the physical reality that the bead signal is
// read from the bead-laden channel area, not from a mobile
// droplet removed to a detection zone.

detectCh16         = dispense 1 units of AlexaCRP
detectCh1          = dispense 1 units of AlexaCRP

bindingSignal      = detect crpBindingDetection on detectCh16 for 30s
ch1Signal          = detect crpBindingDetection on detectCh1 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: CRP binding QC gate (ch16 - ~4000x factor)
// Pass (BB2): bindingSignal > 0 -> Alexa-488 fluorescence
//             above background (40-50 AU) detected on beads;
//             CRP binding confirmed at high-conc end.
//             Dispose ch16 detect volume.
// Fail (BB3): bindingSignal <= 0 -> no fluorescence above
//             background; concentration or binding failed.
//             Drain ch16 detect volume.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (bindingJoin).
// ============================================================

if (bindingSignal > 0) {
    dispose detectCh16
} else {
    drain detectCh16
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: bindingJoin
// Dispose ch16 QC signal. Control falls into ch1 QC branch
// (BB5/BB6) to confirm low-concentration end of dynamic range.
// ============================================================

dispose bindingSignal

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: CRP binding QC gate (ch1 - ~100x factor)
// Pass (BB5): ch1Signal > 0 -> weak but detectable Alexa-488
//             signal above background (signals 56-66 AU;
//             background 40-50 AU; Fig. 5a, paper).
//             Dynamic range low end confirmed. Dispose ch1.
// Fail (BB6): ch1Signal <= 0 -> no detectable signal at ch1;
//             drain ch1 detect volume.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (ch1Signal > 0) {
    dispose detectCh1
} else {
    drain detectCh1
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose ch1 QC signal droplet. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose ch1Signal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
